          "content": "Recognize a mineral by integrating chemistry, structure, geological origin, and replicable measurements rather than a single memorable color. A damaged sample, aggregate, or synthetic specimen can provide useful mineralogical information even when it cannot be named confidently by an unaided observer. A robust classification is an evidence-based claim with an explicit uncertainty budget. This unit connects five distinct questions rather than memorizing five disconnected lists of features. The repeated aim is to move from an observation, through a process explanation, to a testable mineralogical inference. Each topic includes at least one case in which several different explanations fit the initial evidence, so that the method teaches disciplined uncertainty rather than an automatic answer key.",
