          "heading": "Purpose and starting assumptions",
          "content": "Relate translation, symmetry, crystal morphology, reciprocal-space planes, and imperfections. A crystal is a three-dimensional periodic structure, but natural crystals may be bent, intergrown, fractured, twinned, compositionally zoned, or too small for a recognizably euhedral shape. This unit connects five distinct questions rather than memorizing five disconnected lists of features. The repeated aim is to move from an observation, through a process explanation, to a testable mineralogical inference. Each topic includes at least one case in which several different explanations fit the initial evidence, so that the method teaches disciplined uncertainty rather than an automatic answer key.",
